          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What the paint costs</h3>

          <p>
            At the time of writing, budget ceiling paints run roughly $25 to $35 a gallon, mid-range paints $35 to $50, and premium ceiling paints $55 to $80 or more at full price. Sherwin-Williams and Benjamin Moore products are often discounted in their regular sales. Textured ceilings can take twice as much paint, so buy extra.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Tools, primer and professional labor</h3>

          <p>
            Set aside roughly $30 to $70 more for roller covers, a frame, an extension pole, an angled brush, drop cloths, painter's tape and stain-blocking primer. Hiring the job out usually costs more per square foot for ceilings than for walls because of the extra setup and difficulty, often a few hundred dollars per room depending on region, ceiling height and condition.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Buy it all at once and box it</h3>

          <p>
            Purchase all the paint in one trip and box it, pouring the cans together in a large bucket so color and sheen match across the whole ceiling. Keep a little leftover, labeled with the room and date, for touch-ups, which blend best when they come from the original batch.
          </p>
